{"name":"Early Frost","hex":"#dae3e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"early","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.","Arriving a time before expected; sooner than on time."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shift (scheduled work period) that takes place early in the day."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early"},{"term":"frost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover of minute ice crystals on objects that are exposed to the air. Frost is formed by the same process as dew, except that the temperature of the frosted object is below freezing.","The cold weather that causes these ice crystals to form."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with frost.","To become covered with frost."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frost"}],"entries":[{"title":"Early Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Early Frost is a 1982 Australian thriller film starring Guy Doleman, Jon Blake, Diana McLean and David Franklin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Early_Frost"},{"title":"Frost","blocks":[{"text":"Frost is a layer of ice on a solid surface, which forms from water vapor that deposits onto a freezing surface. Frost forms when the air contains more water vapor than it can normally hold at a specific temperature. The process is similar to the formation of dew, except it occurs below the freezing point of water typically without crossing through a liquid state."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg/330px-Saint-Amant_16_Gel%C3%A9e_blanche_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frost"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg/500px-Nevada-Apartadero-Merida-Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb